{{!
    @template mod_presenterai/rubric_preview

    The activity settings form's read only view of the rubric the activity
    will use: each criterion with its description and its five written levels
    (or its maximum when it has none), and an Edit rubric link once the
    activity exists. There's no editing here.

    One block per choice the form can reach, keyed by data-previewfor
    ('type:<presentation type>' for the automatic rubric of that type,
    'rubric:<id>' for a stored rubric). mod_presenterai/form shows the one
    that matches the presentation type and rubric selects and hides the rest;
    without the script the one matching the saved values (shown) is visible.
    defaults is the JSON the script fills the form from when the type changes.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * defaults - JSON: presentation type => mode, minseconds, maxseconds, slidesenabled, topics.
    * previews - List of {key, shown, title (HTML), criteria, editurl, editnote}. Each criterion has name,
      description, haslevels, levels (score, label, description), maxtext and feedbackonly.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "defaults": "{\"practice\":{\"mode\":\"video\",\"minseconds\":20,\"maxseconds\":90,\"slidesenabled\":0,\"topics\":[\"Introduce yourself\"]}}",
        "previews": [
            {
                "key": "type:practice",
                "shown": true,
                "title": "Built-in rubric for this presentation type",
                "criteria": [
                    {
                        "name": "Delivery",
                        "description": "Speaking clearly at a comfortable pace.",
                        "haslevels": true,
                        "levels": [
                            {"score": 5, "label": "Excellent", "description": "Clear and confident."},
                            {"score": 1, "label": "Not yet", "description": "Not clear enough to follow yet."}
                        ],
                        "maxtext": "Scored out of 5",
                        "feedbackonly": false
                    }
                ],
                "editurl": "https://example.com/mod/presenterai/rubric.php?id=3&action=edit&preset=practice",
                "editnote": ""
            }
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="mod-presenterai-rubricpreview" data-region="presenterai-rubricpreview" data-defaults="{{defaults}}">
    {{#previews}}
    <div class="mod-presenterai-rubricpreview-item" data-previewfor="{{key}}"{{^shown}} hidden{{/shown}}>
        <p class="mb-2"><strong>{{{title}}}</strong></p>
        {{#criteria}}
        <div class="mod-presenterai-rubricpreview-criterion mb-3">
            <h4 class="h6 mb-1">{{name}}{{#feedbackonly}} <span class="badge badge-info bg-info">{{#str}}feedback_criterion_notcounted, mod_presenterai{{/str}}</span>{{/feedbackonly}}</h4>
            {{#description}}<p class="small mb-1">{{description}}</p>{{/description}}
            {{#haslevels}}
            <table class="table table-sm table-bordered small mb-0">
                <caption class="accesshide">{{#str}}rubriclevels, mod_presenterai{{/str}}</caption>
                <tbody>
                    {{#levels}}
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="row" class="text-nowrap">{{score}} {{label}}</th>
                        <td>{{description}}</td>
                    </tr>
                    {{/levels}}
                </tbody>
            </table>
            {{/haslevels}}
            {{^haslevels}}
            <p class="small mb-0">{{maxtext}}</p>
            {{/haslevels}}
        </div>
        {{/criteria}}
        {{#editurl}}
        <p class="mb-0"><a href="{{editurl}}">{{#str}}rubricpreview_edit, mod_presenterai{{/str}}</a></p>
        {{/editurl}}
        {{^editurl}}
        {{#editnote}}
        <p class="small mb-0">{{editnote}}</p>
        {{/editnote}}
        {{/editurl}}
    </div>
    {{/previews}}
</div>
